WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.934
-Our next guest will be at The Comedy Attic

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.968
in Bloomington, Indiana, August 12th and 13th.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.734
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:10.968
please welcome the very funny Emil Wakim!

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:18.801
♪♪

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.300
-Thank you so much. Hello.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:27.267
Oh, thank you. Thank you.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:31.400
Thank you so much. Thanks. Thanks.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.734
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.400
Alright? Cool?

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.367
So, here's what I think about Israel and Palestine. Uh...

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.968
No, I'm kidding. That'd be a crazy way to take the show.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.234
No. No.

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:45.767
I don't know. I don't know.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.567
I know it looks like I would know.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:51.534
But I do not know.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.234
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:56.367
It's weird not knowing, especially when you look like

00:00:56.367 --> 00:01:00.400
both sides of the conflict in the Middle East.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.501
But I'm very happy to be here. I hope you guys are doing well.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.934
And -- Yeah. Yes.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:13.100
And by "guys," obviously I mean half not that.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.200
Uh, it's a weird thing we do.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.267
We just say, "Hey, guys," to a whole group of people.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.033
I don't know what the better term is, either.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.334
Like, I don't know what, like,

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:23.567
the more accepting, encompassing term is.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.767
Like, some people think it's "y'all."

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:29.801
But it's -- it's not. No, it's --

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.467
"Y'all" with that twang on it.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.467
Like, no minority has ever heard,

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.934
"Where y'all from?"

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:41.334
and thought, "This is gonna turn out well for me."

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:46.734
[ Laughs ]

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.934
Like, okay, I saw a lady

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:53.133
wearing a shirt that said, "Y'all Means All."

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:57.067
And I was like, "No, it doesn't."

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.334
It doesn't.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:01.267
A sign that says, "Y'all are welcome here,"

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.868
does not mean all are welcome here.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.467
It's less.

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:10.100
Like, it's less in the way that --

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.367
Like, you know when you see someone holding a sign

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.501
that says, "all lives matter,"

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.334
yeah, they mean y'all lives.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:20.267
Like, that's the difference.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.968
It's tense racially. You can feel it in the country.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:31.400
It's very tense.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.667
I worry all the time about people in my life, you know?

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.334
Because, like, my dad is an immigrant,

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:38.200
so I worry every day that someone is going to treat him

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.868
poorly because of the color of his skin.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.601
And my mom is a white lady from the suburbs,

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.734
so I worry that she's gonna be the one to do it.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.033
[ Laughs ]

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.067
Dude!

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:58.501
Every time my mom starts yelling at my dad for something now,

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:02.000
I just start recording her on my cellphone.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.467
I'm like, "You're getting canceled, okay?"

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.300
[ Laughs ]

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.567
We're trying to be better now. We're trying to be good.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:11.734
It's great.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.167
You know, we're in this movement now

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:14.801
where, like, people, like, love diversity

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:16.267
and, like, everyone loves culture.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.000
It's amazing. It's very beautiful.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.100
It's just -- It's exhausting to me now

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.801
to always have to be, like, proud of my culture.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.267
Because I never learned how to growing up.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:25.701
Like, all I learned how to do growing up

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.634
was how to push it away to get by.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.834
So now it's just frustrating because now I have, like,

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.734
these, like, woke friends that are mad at me

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:36.234
for not being as authentic as they want me to be.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.067
They're like, "Why don't you know how to speak Arabic?"

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.467
And I'm like, "Because I wanted to come

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.267
to your birthday party in fifth grade, okay?

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.300
That's why."

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:47.934
I mean...

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.367
[ Laughs ]

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:53.834
Yeah. No one wanted a kid speaking Arabic at laser tag.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:58.067
Like, I don't know if you remember.

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.300
It was tense.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:07.367
I hope it's genuine.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.901
That's all I'll say for this movement.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.334
I hope it's genuine change.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:11.567
I just don't think it is.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.067
It's just -- It's too rapid of a shift.

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.534
You know? It's hard for me to get used to.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:17.334
We went really polar opposites.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:20.067
Like, I'm 24, and I remember a different America.

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:22.934
That's how recently no one cared about this.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.200
I remember as a kid, like,

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.133
I started shaving when I was in fourth grade.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.334
When I would go get my hair cut, I would have them thin it out

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:34.968
with shears so it wouldn't be curly.

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:38.100
If my parents packed me lunch with hummus in it,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.367
I would throw it all away

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:44.801
because I would rather go hungry than be persecuted.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:48.467
I hated, like, who I was. You know that feeling?

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:52.834
I have vivid memories of kids looking me in my eyes

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.634
and saying, "Don't think we'll ever forget

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:58.701
what you did to our country."

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:02.267
And now things are different.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.000
I was at the grocery store,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.367
and I saw pumpkin-spice flavored hummus.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:15.801
And I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:17.767
They forgot."

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:22.267
My name's Emil Wakim. Thank you guys very much.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.968
♪♪

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:30.501
-Emil Wakim! There you go. Not too bad.

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:33.467
Standing "O." Emil Wakim. You look sharp, buddy.

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.334
-Thank you. -He'll be at The Comedy Attic

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.467
in Bloomington, Indiana, August 12th and 13th!

